> Signaling, not biology. ==The argument is *not* that owning the "right" objects makes you better — it's that the everyday objects you carry are visible proxies for whether you organize your life.== Maintained, coherent everyday carry signals organizational competence. Mismatched, neglected carry signals the opposite. The objects don't matter; the *signal of attention to them* does.

