## B. The wallet & FinTech baseline

The era of the thick leather wallet stuffed with paper receipts is over and has been for at least a decade. The current minimum:

> [!check] The wallet minimum
> - **Slim cardholder.** Magnetic or simple leather slot card holder — 4–6 cards maximum, no coin compartment, no paper receipt pocket. RM 40–300 depending on tier (Bellroy, Bonia, local artisans on Etsy MY).
> - **eWallet primary, physical card backup.** Touch 'n Go eWallet for daily payments, GrabPay or Boost for promotional cashback, MAE by Maybank for QR transfers. Carry one debit card and one credit card physical as backup.
> - **Receipt discipline.** Receipts go in the phone (email, photo, or app), not in the wallet. Empty the wallet every Sunday.

### Credit cards as infrastructure, not status

==The argument is not "get a credit card to look successful." It is that credit cards are a free infrastructure layer that does several useful jobs at once:==[^3]

- **Automated expense tracking.** Statement provides a categorized, searchable record of every transaction.
- **Reward optimization.** Cashback / miles / points are a 1–3% rebate on spend you would do anyway.
- **Credit profile.** Disciplined use builds the credit score you need for housing or business financing later.
- **Fraud protection.** Charge disputes are far easier on credit than on debit.

> [!tip] The Malaysian credit-card starter stack
> - **One general cashback card** — Maybank 2 Cards / CIMB Cash Rebate Platinum / HSBC Visa Signature.
> - **One travel/miles card** *if* you travel often — Citi Premier Miles, Maybank World, AmBank Enrich Visa Infinite. Skip if you fly <4 times a year.
> - **Pay in full every month.** ==Carrying a balance kills the entire economic case.== APR on revolving credit-card debt in Malaysia sits at 15–18% — the cashback rebate of 1–3% never beats it. Pay in full or do not use the card.

### The cash question

Carrying a thick wad of physical cash signals neither wealth nor sophistication; it signals friction. Carry **RM 100–200 in physical cash maximum** as backup for hawker stalls, parking attendants, and emergencies. Everything else is digital.

