## The coherence rule

The single rule that ties this article together:

> [!check] Match the metals, match the leathers, match the maintenance
> - **Metals match across the body** — watch buckle, belt buckle, ring (if worn), bag hardware. Silver-tone all-silver, gold-tone all-gold. ==The mismatched metal is the most common, most fixable signaling tell.==
> - **Leathers harmonize** — shoes, belt, watch strap, bag. Not necessarily identical, but in the same tonal family. Black shoes + tan watch strap + dark brown belt is incoherent.
> - **Maintenance level is uniform across the carry.** A pristine watch on a frayed strap, a clean shirt with a scuffed leather bag — these clashes are louder than any individual upgrade. ==Upgrade evenly across the carry; do not let one item lap the rest.==

This is the actionable preview of [[Part 7.0 - The 1% Cleanliness Audit & The Foundation Gate|Part 7.0]] — the cleanliness audit is where these coherence checks become a weekly ritual.

